course: dictionary
lesson: 10964
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Waltz can be a dance, a piece of music, or a way of walking in. The words around it show you which meaning it has.
explain: «In 3/4 time each bar holds three crotchet beats, the swaying feel of a waltz.» Here a waltz is a kind of music with three beats in each bar. Count it aloud: ONE-two-three, ONE-two-three.
explain: «He waltzed in late.» Here waltzed means walked in carelessly, as if nothing mattered. The word late is the clue: he did not seem to care that he was not on time.
fact: A waltz is a smooth dance for two people who turn round and round together.
fact: A waltz has three beats in each bar: ONE-two-three.
fact: «3/4 means three crotchet beats in each bar, which gives the swaying feel of a waltz.»
fact: «Waltzing» in «Waltzing Matilda» means wandering the land with your swag, which is a bedroll.
fact: «She waltzed through the test.» means she did it very easily.
exercise: «3/4 means three crotchet beats in each bar, which gives the swaying feel of a waltz.» What does 3/4 mean? | Three rests in a row | Three dancers on the floor | *Three crotchet beats in each bar | Three different songs at once
exercise: «He waltzed in late.» What does waltzed mean here? | Ran in, out of breath | Danced in a smooth circle | *Walked in carelessly, as if nothing mattered | Sang loudly on the stage
exercise: «She waltzed through the test.» What does waltzed through mean? | *Did it very easily | Failed it badly | Read it slowly and carefully | Danced across the hall
test: «Johann Strauss wrote The Blue Danube, a famous waltz.» Which meaning of waltz is this? | A slow walk through a park | *A piece of music for a smooth dance in three beats | A kind of small boat
test: «The thief waltzed off with the prize.» What does waltzed off with mean? | *Took it away easily, as if it was nothing | Gave the prize back politely | Danced happily with the prize | Threw the prize in the river
exam: Which sentence uses waltz as a verb? | *Matt waltzed out of the door | The band played a waltz | The waltz was smooth and slow | A waltz has three beats in each bar
